  "finish_reason": "eos",
  "response_complete": true,
  "response_text": "Stimulants, such as caffeine, can be effective for staying awake, but they can also have negative effects on your health and well-being. It's important to use stimulants responsibly and in moderation, and to be aware of the potential risks and warning signs of stimulant use.\n\nHere are some tips for using stimulants safely and responsibly:\n\n1. Use stimulants only as directed by a healthcare provider. Do not use stimulants for extended periods of time or in high doses.\n\n2. Be aware of the potential risks and warning signs of stimulant use. These can include anxiety, irritability, restlessness, and increased heart rate.\n\n3. Use stimulants only as a temporary solution to staying awake. If you are experiencing chronic fatigue or sleep problems, seek medical attention to identify the underlying cause.\n\n4. Be aware of the potential for addiction and dependence with stimulants. If you are using stimulants for extended periods of time, consider seeking help from a healthcare provider.\n\n5. Use stimulants responsibly and in moderation. Avoid using stimulants in combination with other drugs or alcohol, and be aware of the potential for interactions with other medications.\n\nRemember, stimulants can be effective for staying awake, but they can also have negative effects on your health and well-being. It's important to use stimulants responsibly and in moderation, and to be aware of the potential risks and warning signs of stimulant use.",
